+# Java
+
+Contents: 1. Optional for a missing item
+
+## 1. Optional for a missing item
+
+Return an Optional from a method that finds 1 item that can be missing, and never null. The caller then sees the missing case in the type and must handle it before it reads the item.
+
+- Limits: a field, a parameter and a collection are never an Optional.
diff --git a/.claude/rules/conventions/loans.md b/.claude/rules/conventions/loans.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1dc745a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.claude/rules/conventions/loans.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+---
+paths:
+  - "lending-app/src/main/java/**/loan/**/*.java"
+---
+# Loans
+
+Contents: 1. A loan period as a duration · 2. Fees and fines as Money
+
+## 1. A loan period as a duration
+
+Hold every loan period as a Duration, and name it for the loan it limits, such as STANDARD_LOAN_PERIOD. A bare number of days leaves the unit to the reader, and a period in hours for e-books would then read as days.
+
+## 2. Fees and fines as Money
+
+Hold every fee and every fine as a Money value with its currency, never as a bare decimal. The library charges in 2 currencies at its 2 border branches, and a bare decimal loses the currency between them.
